description:
### Describe the Bug

After adopting RuntimeContext to be used across instructions and model, I noticed that if `generateTitle` does not get the RuntimeContext, meaning that if no fall-back model is picked then it will fail.

This might be intended behavior and if so, it might just be a case of documenting this.

### Steps To Reproduce

Set up memory to generateTitles, e.g:
```javascript
export const memory = new Memory({
  storage: postgresStore,
  vector: new PgVector({
    connectionString: process.env.DATABASE_URL,
  }),
  embedder: openai.embedding("text-embedding-3-small"),
  options: {
    semanticRecall: true,
    lastMessages: 40,
    threads: {
      generateTitle: true,
    },
    workingMemory: {
      use: "tool-call",
      enabled: true,
    },
  },
});
```

Define an agent with dynamic model, e.g:
```javascript
export const myAgent = new Agent({
  name: "My Agent",
  instructions: ({ runtimeContext }) => {
    const config = configFromRuntimeContext(runtimeContext);
    if (!config.instructions) {
      throw Error("Missing instructions.");
    }
    return config.instructions;
  },
  model: ({ runtimeContext }) => {
    const config = configFromRuntimeContext(runtimeContext);
    try {
      const model = modelFromConfig(config);
      return model;
    } catch {
      // Mastra needs a model to generate titles (that process will not get runtimeContext)
      return openai("gpt-4o");
    }
  },
  memory,
});
```

In case I did not have that catch in the model part, `generateTitle` would fail as it does not get the RuntimeContext when resolving the model to use generating titles.

### Expected Behavior

I'm not sure.. perhaps title generation should have its own model? Depending on how RuntimeContext works, it could also have that being passed? Alternatively this should be clear from the docs if this is intended behavior.

### Environment Information

Latest (stable) versions as of today

### Verification

- [x] I have searched the existing issues to make sure this is not a duplicate
- [x] I have included sufficient information for the team to reproduce and understand the issue
